VTFLib++'s VTFLib/Resource.rc includes afxres.h, which only ships with the
optional MFC component of the Visual Studio build tools. The resource script
contains no MFC resources, so winres.h (Windows SDK) is the correct
replacement for non-MFC projects. This changes only how the resource compiler
parses the DLL version resource; library behavior is unchanged.

Applied to the pinned VTFLib++ submodule revision (master commit b27ecd3,
"Fix incorrect component order for ARGB8888", which includes the
BC4/BC5/BC6H_UNSIGNED id corrections from "Update enum order for BC6H
onwards").

Automatic, idempotent application:
    cmake -P thirdparty/patches/apply_vtflib_patches.cmake
or from the viewer build tree:
    cmake --build build --target vtflib_apply_patch

Manual application from the parent repository root:
    git -C thirdparty/vtflib apply ../patches/vtflib-resource-winres.patch
diff --git a/VTFLib/Resource.rc b/VTFLib/Resource.rc
index 3b5dbdf..8c35abc 100644
--- a/VTFLib/Resource.rc
+++ b/VTFLib/Resource.rc
@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@
 //
 // Generated from the TEXTINCLUDE 2 resource.
 //
-#include "afxres.h"
+// VMTViewer patch: afxres.h requires the optional MFC component; this script
+// uses no MFC resources, so winres.h (Windows SDK) is the correct replacement.
+#include "winres.h"
 
 /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 #undef APSTUDIO_READONLY_SYMBOLS
